{"name":"Blue Blood","hex":"#6b7f81","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue blood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Noble or aristocratic ancestry.","An aristocrat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_blood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nobility","blocks":[{"text":"Nobility is a social class found in many societies that have an aristocracy. It is normally appointed by and ranked immediately below royalty. Nobility has often been an estate of the realm with many exclusive functions and characteristics. The characteristics associated with nobility may constitute substantial advantages over or relative to non-nobles or simply formal functions, and vary by country and by era. Membership in the nobility, including rights and responsibilities, is typically hereditary and patrilineal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Queen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg/330px-Queen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobility","wikidata":"Q134737"},{"title":"Blood","blocks":[{"text":"Blood is a specialized form of connective tissue and body fluid in the circulatory system of humans and other vertebrates that delivers necessary substances such as nutrients and oxygen to the cells of the body, and transports metabolic waste products away from those same cells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg/330px-Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood","wikidata":"Q7873"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Queen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg/500px-Queen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Queen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg/1280px-Queen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Queen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg/500px-Queen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The House of Lords is the upper legislature of the Parliament of the United Kingdom and is filled with members that are selected from the aristocracy (those ennobled only for their individual lives).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQueen_Anne_in_the_House_of_Lords.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7f/Crusader_cavalry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7f/Crusader_cavalry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Nobility offered protection in exchange for service.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F